# Build context for the Dockerfile in this directory.
#
# Allowlist: everything is excluded first and only the build inputs are
# re-included, so new files (secrets, models, local data) stay out of the
# context by default. This excludes, among others: .git, .github, .venv,
# .claude/, task/, tests/, docs/, data/ except the source list (the container
# downloads the corpus and builds the index into named volumes, see
# compose.yaml), IDE folders, .env files, and the Docker files
# themselves.
#
# Adapted from the asset dockerignore-example of the docker-project-foundations
# skill (https://github.com/docker/skills), licensed under the Apache License,
# Version 2.0 (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). Modified for this
# project: rewritten as an allowlist for a uv-based Python build.

*

# Build inputs. pyproject.toml declares readme = "README.md" and
# license-files = ["LICENSE"], so building the project needs both files.
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!.python-version
!README.md
!LICENSE
!src/
# Include only the public UI theme, never Streamlit secrets.
!.streamlit/
.streamlit/*
!.streamlit/config.toml
# The source list of the corpus download, read at start-up.
!data/sources.toml

# Never send these, even from inside a re-included path such as src/.

# Python caches and build leftovers
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Environment files, secrets and credentials
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.npmrc
**/.pypirc
**/.netrc
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/.streamlit/secrets.toml

# Local vector stores and model weights
**/chroma_db/
**/.chroma/
**/*.gguf

# Editor and OS files
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/*~
